%%%
# A 1000-step drifting random walk

Step k is $x_k \sim \mathrm{Normal}(x_{k-1} + \delta, s)$ with $x_0 = 0$, a
`markovchain` with the drift and the step scale as additional arguments. The
initial state carries no density, so the trajectory has 1000 terms. The
observed path is a fixed deterministic curve.
%%%
flatppl_compat = "0.1"

t = linspace(0.0, 20.0, 1000)
x_data = sin.(t) .+ 0.05 .* t
step(prev, drift, scale) = Normal(prev + drift, scale)
